00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.000
Shannon Lee: Yes, I can.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:54.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay, perfect. So everything so far looks really good with the click-through rate. That sometimes, it's normally not an issue, but as long as we're getting relevant clicks to your site, and normally we have a three, the three to five percent range is like industry standard of people seeing your ad clicking and getting on.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:05:05.000
Carmen Cruickshank: So this definitely shows people, you know, have high intent for that. Let's see. And then search impression share. You're getting a good percent of people in your area looking for a photographer for weddings.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:15.000
Carmen Cruickshank: So that's great. And I'm just looking at July, so just the past two weeks, just to keep it recent. Uh, but I could extend the view to all of June and July, just to get a comparison.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:28.000
Carmen Cruickshank: But yeah, the cost per conversion is also one of the biggest things I look at, so let's say if you had two leads, but it was, like, $20 cost per lead, that's a lot different, you know, than $120. Of course, we definitely want it.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:38.000
Carmen Cruickshank: I'd say at the 50 range. I think 50 is what I see on average for Google for all accounts, and there's definitely several factors that go into decreasing the cost per conversion.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:42.000
Carmen Cruickshank: But yeah, this is just a good starting point just to see what's going on.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:51.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Um, and then as for conversion rates, so people that go onto your site and then become a lead, we definitely want that at 3-5%, so this is below average.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:57.000
Carmen Cruickshank: But yeah, this is just a metric, and then after we can diagnose and figure out what to do to improve it.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:06:07.000
Carmen Cruickshank: And then right now, I also have you on maximize clicks, so just trying to get the cheapest cost per click, which is $2, just for general Florida, excluding the panhandle. Uh…

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:14.000
Carmen Cruickshank: I would want to take it to maximize conversions, because sometimes that does get the ball rolling and just gets all these conversions onto…

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:25.000
Carmen Cruickshank: you know, your CRM. Uh, but then that also could increase the cost per click, so it would be less people per day. But Google, out of knowing the type of people that are converting.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:33.000
Carmen Cruickshank: they can target those people more, so it might be less clicks, less visitors to the site, but more leads. That makes sense.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:41.000
Shannon Lee: Yeah, that does. So, um, I should go and I should change it to… from maximize clicks to…

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:43.000
Shannon Lee: Uh, maximize conversions.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:53.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Uh, I think we could wait… maybe 2 more weeks, and then we could do maximize conversions. I could also just change it over the call and show you how to do that. Uh…

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:55.000
Carmen Cruickshank: But yeah, I think…

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:57.000
